userStories.description:
**Goal** — Create the branded `WorktreeId`, the story derivation, and the path/branch/ref producers in one module, and add the static gate that fails when any other file spells a `.nax-wt` path or a `nax/` branch.

**Motivation** — Fifteen production sites spell worktree paths, branch names or orphan refs (five through a parameter, ten by direct string construction). The current `bakeoff/worktree-id.ts` already implements the sanitize/cap/hash-suffix derivation for bakeoff worktrees; this story moves the shared parts into one module and adds one producer per spelling so the SSOT is checkable rather than remembered.

**Approach** — Compose an opaque, feature-scoped worktree identity; give every spelling one producer; and gate the spellings statically. A branded identity type alone is not sufficient (the eight direct-construction sites have no parameter type to constrain), so the design has three parts: (1) one producer per spelling — `storyWorktreePath(projectRoot, worktreeId)`, `storyBranchName(worktreeId)`, `naxOrphanRefName(worktreeId)` are the only functions that spell `.nax-wt/<id>`, `nax/<id>` and `refs/nax/orphan/<id>`; (2) a branded `WorktreeId` (a `string` carrying a unique type tag), produced only by `deriveStoryWorktreeId` or `deriveBakeoffWorktreeId`; (3) a static gate `scripts/check-worktree-id-ssot.ts` that fails when a literal `.nax-wt` path segment or `nax/`-prefixed branch string is built outside the identity module, carrying an explicit allowlist as well as a per-line comment escape hatch (like `scripts/check-feature-dir-ssot.ts:28, :36`). The allowlist members — the producers themselves; `src/runtime/packages.ts` (`:109` and `:237` compare the first path segment; ACs pin their unchanged behaviour); `src/utils/gitignore.ts:62` (gitignore entry); `src/review/runner/index.ts:247` (ignore regex); `src/precheck/checks-git.ts:55` (porcelain-status regex); `src/precheck/checks-warnings.ts:235` (ignore entry); `src/bakeoff/preflight.ts:18` (composes the separate `nax/bakeoff-` branch namespace) — are consumer sites whose spelling must stay exactly as it is.

**Scope** — In: move shared sanitize/cap/hash-suffix derivation from `src/bakeoff/worktree-id.ts` into `src/worktree/worktree-id.ts`; introduce branded `WorktreeId` type and `deriveStoryWorktreeId`/`deriveBakeoffWorktreeId`/`storyWorktreePath`/`storyBranchName`; add `scripts/check-worktree-id-ssot.ts`; register the gate in `package.json` so `bun run check:all-without-biome` invokes it and `scripts/check-gate-reachability.ts` is satisfied; ensure the bakeoff helper's returned values are unchanged for the same inputs.
Out: changing `WorktreeManager.create`/`remove`, `MergeEngine.merge`/`mergeAll`, `naxOrphanRefName`'s parameter type, or any execution-layer site spelling — those belong to US-002 and US-003.

**Interface**
```typescript
// src/worktree/worktree-id.ts (new)
export type WorktreeId = string & { readonly __brand: "WorktreeId" };

export function deriveStoryWorktreeId(feature: string, storyId: string): WorktreeId;
export function deriveBakeoffWorktreeId(feature: string, profile: string): WorktreeId;
export function storyWorktreePath(projectRoot: string, worktreeId: WorktreeId): string;
export function storyBranchName(worktreeId: WorktreeId): string;
```
The natural identity is `story-<feature>-<storyId>`, sanitized to `validateStoryId`'s alphabet and capped at 64 characters, with a distinguishing hash suffix when truncation would collide two distinct inputs. Depth stays at two path segments. The `bakeoff-` namespace stays disjoint from `story-`.

**Goal** — Change `WorktreeManager.create`/`remove`, `MergeEngine.merge`/`mergeAll` and `naxOrphanRefName` to accept `WorktreeId` and to take every spelling from US-001's producers, while keeping `MergeResult.storyId` and `StoryDependencies` keyed by raw story IDs.

**Motivation** — The five parameter sites in `src/worktree/manager.ts`, `src/worktree/merge.ts` and `src/worktree/nax-orphan-ref.ts` are the API surface where a raw story ID becomes a path or branch. If they alone are composed and the eight direct-construction sites under `src/execution/` and `src/bakeoff/` are not, three sites silently fail (iteration-runner's `effectiveWorkdir` resolves to a non-existent directory, the result-handler's `hasWorktree` returns false and disables the BUG-28 evidence path, the orphan-ref writer names a branch that does not exist because of the raw `refs/heads/nax/<storyId>` source). Composition at the API also lets `src/bakeoff/contestant.ts:143` pass an already-composed bakeoff identity through the same `create()` without re-composing.

**Approach** — The branded parameter is required by `WorktreeManager.create`, `WorktreeManager.remove`, `MergeEngine.merge`, `MergeEngine.mergeAll`, and `naxOrphanRefName`; each takes its directory, branch and ref from `storyWorktreePath`/`storyBranchName`/`naxOrphanRefName` (the third name on the same module). `deriveBakeoffWorktreeId` returns `WorktreeId` so `src/bakeoff/contestant.ts:143` keeps typechecking against the branded `create`. The structural `ContestantRunnerDeps.worktreeManager` declaration narrows its `create`/`remove` signatures to take `WorktreeId`. `MergeEngine.mergeAll` receives `Array<{ storyId: string; worktreeId: WorktreeId }>` so each result's `storyId` is the raw story ID while the merge uses the composed branch. `MergeResult.storyId` and `StoryDependencies` stay keyed by raw story IDs (the join keys into `pipelinePassed`, `storyCosts` and `prd.userStories`, and the keys `topologicalSort`/`failedStories` use to order and skip).

**Scope** — In: change the five worktree-API signatures; route their string constructions through US-001's producers; update existing test call sites in `test/integration/worktree/manager.test.ts`, `test/integration/worktree/worktree-merge.test.ts`, `test/unit/worktree/manager.test.ts`, `test/unit/worktree/nax-orphan-ref.test.ts`, `test/unit/execution/merge.test.ts`, `test/integration/bakeoff/coordinator-worktree-isolation.test.ts`, `test/integration/bakeoff/preflight-reclaim.test.ts` to derive an identity before calling.
Out: any direct-construction site under `src/execution/` (iteration-runner.ts:90, parallel-batch.ts:164, merge-conflict-rectify.ts:272, pipeline-result-handler.ts:48/:68/:116/:477, run-initialization.ts:239/:254) and `src/bakeoff/contestant.ts:124` — those belong to US-003.

**Interface**
```typescript
// WorktreeManager.create
//   baseline: create(projectRoot: string, storyId: string): Promise<void>
//   target:   create(projectRoot: string, worktreeId: WorktreeId): Promise<void>
//   directory from storyWorktreePath(projectRoot, worktreeId)
//   branch   from storyBranchName(worktreeId)

// WorktreeManager.remove
//   baseline: remove(projectRoot: string, storyId: string)
//   target:   remove(projectRoot: string, worktreeId: WorktreeId)
//   through the same two producers

// MergeEngine.merge
//   baseline: merge(projectRoot: string, storyId: string): Promise<Omit<MergeResult, "storyId">>
//   target:   merge(projectRoot: string, worktreeId: WorktreeId): Promise<Omit<MergeResult, "storyId">>
//   branch from storyBranchName(worktreeId); return type unchanged

// MergeEngine.mergeAll
//   baseline: mergeAll(projectRoot: string, storyIds: string[], dependencies: StoryDependencies)
//   target:   mergeAll(
//               projectRoot: string,
//               stories: Array<{ storyId: string; worktreeId: WorktreeId }>,
//               dependencies: StoryDependencies,
//             ): Promise<MergeResult[]>
//   dependencies stays keyed by raw story IDs; each MergeResult.storyId stays raw

// naxOrphanRefName
//   baseline: naxOrphanRefName(storyId: string): string  // "refs/nax/orphan/<storyId>"
//   target:   naxOrphanRefName(worktreeId: WorktreeId): string  // "refs/nax/orphan/<worktreeId>"

// ContestantRunnerDeps.worktreeManager (src/bakeoff/contestant.ts:62-66)
//   target:
//     create: (projectRoot: string, worktreeId: WorktreeId) => Promise<unknown>;
//     remove: (projectRoot: string, worktreeId: WorktreeId) => Promise<unknown>;

// deriveBakeoffWorktreeId (src/bakeoff/worktree-id.ts:29)
//   baseline: deriveBakeoffWorktreeId(feature: string, profile: string): string
//   target:   deriveBakeoffWorktreeId(feature: string, profile: string): WorktreeId
```
